# 0079-cloud-subfolder-checks-and-cover-on-landing.patch -- the NAS / Cloud page: (1) the games of a source's subfolders get exactly the checks of the folder's own games; (2) a game added from the
# NAS or a Files folder of the Cloud page gets its cover as soon as its file has landed, like a local import.
# Applies after 0078. UNTESTED ON DEVICE, IN THE SIMULATOR AND AGAINST A REAL SFTP SERVER OR FILE PROVIDER: compiled, and its pure part ran in a host harness (below).
#
# WHY (the owner's field report on the NAS / Cloud page): "pas de vérif des jeux des sous dossiers" and "pas d'ajout de la thumbnail automatiquement".
#   What a listed game gets, read from the code (0051, 0062, 0065, 0067, 0077): every check keys on the CloudFile's NAME and reads through its REMOTE: "In the library" / greyed (Cloud.CloudOnlyGames:
#   the name against Documents), Download / Download and build with the update and DLC (Cloud.DownloadSet, GameAppUi.UpdateFor / DlcFor: the title id and [vN] of the NAME), "also in the cloud"
#   (Cloud.CloudCopyOf), "In NAS · size" (the listing's size), the cover before the download (FetchCloudIcons: games/<id>/icon.jpg, the id from the NAME), after the download the local passes
#   (FetchMissingIcons: the control NCA's icon, and the id read from the package when the name has none, 0051; FetchMissingNupIcons: a .nup's own icon, 0065), "Choose a cover…" (0065).
#   On the NAS, 0077 gives a subfolder's file its own name and its real path, so it already goes through that same code; three things still left subfolder games without their checks:
#   (a) a file whose name carries no [title id] (common when the game's folder carries the name: "<game>/<game>.nsz") got no id while it was only in the cloud: FetchCloudIcons skipped it,
#       so no cover, no version, no update / DLC pairing (its update listed as a game of its own) until it was downloaded -- while a LOCAL file without an id gets it from the package (0051);
#   (b) a Files folder of the Cloud page (iCloud Drive, ...) was read at its top level only (Directory.EnumerateFiles): the games of its subfolders were not listed at all;
#   (c) the cover after an add: (i) "Download and build" starts its build in the same main-thread turn as the coalesced redraw, so the icon passes (never while a build runs) skipped the game
#       for the whole build; (ii) a "no icon" marker written by the CLOUD pass (any failed remote read, a timeout included, wrote icon.none) was checked against prod.keys' time only, so the
#       downloaded file was never read; (iii) a .nup's marker is checked against the file's modification time, which a clone keeps from the source.
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#   * GameAppCover.cs, CoverPass (pure, no UIKit; the harness compiles it): ReaderFor (a .nup: its own reader, no keys; .nsp .xci .nsz: the package's, with prod.keys; an update or a DLC: none, the
#     library shows its base game), Once (each landed name once, any case), Run (the pass over the landed files: not a game / no keys / a stub / its icon here already / a build running: no read;
#     else ONE read by the given reader; a build that starts meanwhile stops the pass, the refresh passes read the rest after it), MarkerStands (a "no icon" marker stands only when it is not older
#     than prod.keys -- or the .nup itself -- AND not older than the file's landing, the import ledger's time), LandedAt, BaseIdFromControl (a control NCA's id names a base game only when its low
#     12 bits are 0), CloudOutcomeOf (a failed remote read leaves no marker), Line (the log line; a package with no icon is said once, as a fact: "... none: the package carries no icon (Choose a
#     cover… gives it one)", no alert, no error row), Gate (the one lock every per-file read and write takes).
#   * GameAppMain.cs: FetchMissingIcons' per-file body is now ReadPackageCover(keys, documents, name, out verdict) (same code; under the gate; an icon already there is not read again); the markers go
#     by CoverPass.MarkerStands with the ledger's landing time.
#   * GameAppCoverUi.cs: FetchMissingNupIcons' marker the same; ReadNupCover(documents, name, out verdict) under the gate; CoverPassForLanded(landed, how): on the WORKER that placed the files,
#     right after the last one landed and before the main thread hears of it (so before "Download and build" starts its build), CoverPass.Run with the two per-file readers, `running || stop.Busy`
#     asked before each read, GC.Collect after a package read (as FetchMissingIcons), the lines posted to the log. It writes games/<id>/icon.jpg or a marker, never cover.jpg (the person's cover
#     keeps winning, GameCover.Resolve).
#   * GameAppLibrary.cs: Download (the NAS download, the Files-folder clone or copy; used by Download, Download and build, "Download N from the cloud", "Add it again from <source>") collects each
#     file once it is placed and recorded, and runs CoverPassForLanded after its loop (also when a later file of the set failed). RefreshCloud reads a Files folder with NasScan.ScanFolder over
