#     leaves no marker (remembered for this session only: tried again at the next launch).
#   * GameAppImportUi.cs: the folder flow (RunImportJobs) runs CoverPassForLanded for the files it cloned or copied (not one that was there already), on its worker, before the main thread.
#   * GameAppNas.cs: NasScan.ScanFolder / FolderEntryAt (the Files folder through the same Scan: an iCloud placeholder ".X.nsp.icloud" under its real name, no size); Lines(r, dir, who = "NAS")
#     (the NAS's lines unchanged; the cap's advice is "add a narrower folder" for a Files folder). GameAppIcons.cs: GameIconsStream.Read(keys, stream, out controlTitleId). GameAppUi.cs:
#     SaveTitlesFromContent under a lock (four passes may now save). GameAppCloud.cs: the header comment.
#   * Not changed: the old Import picker (CopyIn) and "Open in iBuilder" (they got their cover from the refresh already, which now also lets a landed file through an old marker); the cloud-only
#     .nup covers (gameapp_nup_icon needs a path; a NAS file has none); one SFTP connection per cloud cover (as before).
#   * New UI texts: none. New log texts (worth a marker in app/verify_ipa.sh, they are in GameApp.dll): "cover: <name> (<how>): <verdict>", "(Choose a cover… gives it one)", "read after the build",
#     "read once prod.keys is added", "its icon is here already", "cover: the pass after the add stopped", "downloaded from the NAS", "added from the ", "cloud: N game files in ... and its M
#     subfolders", "add a narrower folder".
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-21, M1 Pro)
#   * scripts/check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the tree the repository's patches give equals the compiled tree (diff -r).
#   * Compile (the device project build-app.sh step 3 made on 2026-11-21 18:39, copied, sources of the tree, native references left out): `dotnet build gameapp.csproj -c Release -r ios-arm64
#     -t:Compile`: the 0078 tree 0 errors / 40 warnings, with this patch 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code; the new log texts are in the compiled GameApp.dll. No .ipa was made.
#   * Host harness (net11.0, the REAL text of GameAppNas.cs with NAS_LOGIC_ONLY, GameAppCloud.cs, GameAppUi.cs, GameAppCover.cs, GameAppImportFolder.cs, GameAppImport.cs, GameAppSourceRemoval.cs,
#     ...; the UIKit files' text for the wiring): 70 of 70 checks. A game in a NAS subfolder and the same game in the sync folder give the same answer to every check (kind, id, icon and marker
#     paths, playable, greyed, download set with update and DLC, update / DLC pairing, "In NAS · size", "also in the cloud", reader, name) for base, update and DLC; the same for a real Files
#     folder on disk (top level vs subfolder, an iCloud placeholder, "._" files, a hidden, a system, a linked and a deeper folder, a clash); a Files folder with no subfolder lists exactly what
#     the old code listed (names, sizes, Remote); the NAS's log lines unchanged; an id-less name gets its id from a base game's control NCA only, then its icon path and its update pairing; the
#     landed pass: one read per landed game (a name in another case once), none for an update / DLC / .ipa / prod.keys, a stub, an icon already there, no keys (a .nup is still read), a build
#     running (nothing more after it starts); the Ocarina-like .nup with no icon: one plain log line, no alert; the readers' targets are never the custom cover's paths and the cover wins;
#     markers: a cloud marker older than the landing does not stand, the file's own does, no ledger record = as before, newer keys = as before; the wiring: the pass on the Download worker
#     after the loop, before the main thread and before done (Download and build), the landed list filled after the ledger record, the folder flow's worker, `running || stop.Busy`, the shared
#     readers, the gate in the three passes, the cloud pass's id read and its no-marker-on-failure. 23 of 23 mutations of the sources are killed (harness/mutate.py).
#
# NOT VERIFIED
#   * Nothing ran on an iPhone, in the simulator, against an SFTP server or a File Provider: the time a cover read adds before a "Download and build" starts (a control NCA: a few hundred KB;
#     a .nup head: up to ~15 MB) is not measured; that a File Provider lists a subfolder through FileSystemEnumerable as it lists the top level is assumed (0067's folder flow does the same).
#   * That the owner's subfolder games are named without a title id (the likeliest reason, from the code, for "no checks") is an inference: his log was not read here.
#   * GameIconsStream takes the FIRST control NCA of a package; an .xci that carries its update's control NCA first gives an update's id, which is refused (no id until the file is here).
